* ============================================================================
* fullstack_post_refresh_runtime_v1.dts -- DOCFLUSH-20260812-001 (flush v5)
* Phase 4 / Gate 4 post-rebuild capture.
*
* This is the twin of runtime_baseline/fullstack_pre_refresh_runtime_v1.dts.
* Its first block is BYTE-FOR-BYTE the same command sequence so the two
* transcripts diff cleanly; the v5 additions come after, where they cannot
* shift the lines above them.
*
* Run it only AFTER the seven-step sequence in HELP_REFRESH_PACKAGE_V1.md.
* Running it against a store built by a stale exe produces a transcript that
* looks like evidence and is not -- that failure cost v5 a full cycle on
* 2026-08-12.
*
* Run (from D:\code\ccode, ABSOLUTE paths -- datarun pushes cwd to the data root):
*   $run = 'D:\code\ccode\docs\maintenance\lanes\full_stack_documentation\runs\DOCFLUSH-20260812-001\help_refresh'
*   ./datarun.ps1 -CommandLines (Get-Content "$run\fullstack_post_refresh_runtime_v1.dts") |
*     Tee-Object "$run\fullstack_post_refresh_runtime_v1.txt"
*   Set-Location D:\code\ccode
*
* Read-only: every command below reports. Nothing rebuilds, nothing writes HELP.
* ============================================================================
SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

FORMULA "DOCFLUSH-V5-POSTREFRESH-BEGIN"

* --- runtime identity: binds the transcript to an exe and a commit ----------
ABOUT

* --- HELP store as rebuilt ---------------------------------------------------
CMDHELP
CMDHELP TOPICS

* --- structural check of that store -----------------------------------------
CMDHELPCHK

* --- the reference authorities, each reporting its own surface ---------------
DOTHELP
FOXHELP

* --- manual state ------------------------------------------------------------
MANUAL STATUS
MANUAL COUNTS

* --- the 2026-08-12 targets, unchanged from the baseline --------------------
HELP WORKSPACE
HELP ERASE
HELP REGRESSION

* --- the function surface ----------------------------------------------------
HELP FUNCTIONS

* ============================================================================
* v5 ADDITIONS -- everything above this line mirrors the baseline exactly.
* ============================================================================

* --- the two commands whose contracts are NEW since the store was built -----
* SMTP: dotref entry added in 358c14a8a plus a new @dottalk.usage v1 contract
* in src/cli/cmd_smtp.cpp (status: review-needed).
* APPGUI: new @dottalk.usage v1 contract in src/cli/app_gui.cpp.
* Both must resolve. "No help found" for either means the rebuild missed the
* new contracts and Gate 4 FAILS.
HELP SMTP
CMDHELP SMTP
HELP APPGUI
CMDHELP APPGUI

* --- SOURCE distribution, the instrument that settles what moved ------------
* Compare against the addendum's measured table (USAGE_CONTRACT 14914,
* SOURCE_MINER 7503, SHARED_MSG 2637, DOTREF 992, CURATED_DOC 868, EDREF 786,
* FOXREF 665, REGISTRY 462; 28827 lines, 528 topics). foxref.hpp did NOT change
* since the store was built, so FOXREF is expected FLAT; edref.hpp changed
* twice (810686319, aac6b8bdf), so EDREF is expected to MOVE.
CMDHELP SOURCE

FORMULA "DOCFLUSH-V5-POSTREFRESH-END"

QUIT
